#1 StructMark language documentation

This guide covers the StructMark 1.0 core syntax and TypeScript API.

#2 Block syntax

Headings use one to six hash marks. Directive blocks use `@name` and `@end`, with optional attributes.

```text
# Heading

@note [title="A note"]
This is a structured block.
@end
```

#2 Inline syntax

- `*[strong]`: strong emphasis
- `/[emphasis]`: emphasis
- `[[target|label]]`: wiki link
- `[label](https://example.com)`: external link
- `` `code` ``: inline code

#2 TypeScript API

```typescript
import { parseDocument, renderHtml } from "structmark-language-core";

const document = parseDocument(source);
const html = renderHtml(document);
```

#2 Current scope

Version 1.0 includes the language core, AST, semantic diagnostics, serialization, structured tables, and a safe HTML renderer. Editor integrations and visual authoring remain future work.
